# BitBake & KAS Build Outputs
build/
layers/
downloads/
sstate-cache/
.kas/

# Pinned kas-container script, fetched and checksum-verified by "make tool".
# Version and hash live in the Makefile; the script itself is upstream code and
# is deliberately not vendored here.
.kas-container/
*.pyc
*.swp
*~

# The Linux tree that is the SOURCE OF TRUTH for the two front-end drivers
# (ti-ads1299, mcp2210-spi). It is a clone of STMicroelectronics/linux with our
# development branch on top, and it is deliberately NOT content of this
# repository: this repo integrates and builds, that tree holds kernel code, and
# a copy here would be the second source of truth the whole arrangement exists
# to avoid. See docs/implementation_plan_ads1299_upstream.md §2.2 and §2.3.
# Ignored because it sits inside the working directory for convenience - ~5 GB
# and 82k files that a "git add -A" would otherwise stage into the Yocto repo.
linux-med/

# Machine-local build paths (see the "-include local.mk" hook in the Makefile).
# Where this build host keeps downloads/, sstate-cache/ and the build directory
# is a property of the machine, not of the project - the same reason no layer
# names a machine.
local.mk

# Editor / vault local state
.obsidian/

# Update-signing private keys. Only the public keyring (CA certificate + CRL)
# is committed, and it lives in the meta-med-distro layer next to the recipe
# that installs it. Regenerate with scripts/med-pki.sh; the ability to sign a
# bundle devices will accept is deliberately not repository content.
pki/


log/
